+# Lessons: billing
+
+### L-billing-1 Keep money as integer cents in src/billing, never floats
+- **Trigger:** editing amount arithmetic in `src/billing/` (e.g. `total()` in `src/billing/total.py`)
+- **Applies when:** prices or amounts are summed, compared, multiplied or rounded; values are stored or passed between functions
+- **Doesn't apply when:** formatting integer cents into a display string at the output edge (e.g. `f"{cents // 100}.{cents % 100:02d}"`)
+- **Provenance:** user
+- **Date:** 2026-11-11
+- **Evidence:**
+```text
+User correction (2026-11-11):
+"Never use float money in src/billing. We store integer cents; round() on
+floats gave 10.299999 in the March invoice run (npm run invoices showed
+10.29 instead of 10.30)."
+
+Code it applies to, src/billing/total.py:
+    def total(items):
+        return round(sum(i["price"] for i in items), 2)
+```
